  They're not.  The "? enchant armor" spoiler says any random 
piece of worn armor will be enchanted.  In fact, body armor 
covered by other armor will never be enchanted.   e.g.  +5 shirt
worn under any body armor is safe.  So are a +5 shirt and a +5
SDSM worn under a Cloak.  (Whether the cloak is safe depends on
its enchantment. :)

  So only the outermost piece of body armor has any chance of 
being affected by an enchant armor scroll.

  And worn piece of armor is affected is "random", but not
"perfectly random", nor anything like it.  (No, the spoiler
doesn't say "perfectly random")  SpeedEvil did some testing 
showing an uneven distribution.

  Thanks to mrivan (aka More Dread Lord Marvin) on #nethack for 
pointing this out.  More thanks to SpeedEvil on #nethack for 
confirming in the source code and then double-checking in 
wizmode.


